1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:07,500
Global companies process thousands of invoices every day across dozens of languages and currencies.

2
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:14,800
Manual data entry is slow, but standard LLMs hallucinate numbers, causing expensive accounting discrepancies.

3
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:22,000
Watch what happens when we upload a German invoice with European comma decimals.

4
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:29,500
Our kinematic companion, Nova, walks to the document and tracks each pipeline stage in real time.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:39,000
Ingestion, OCR Vision, and Structured Extraction stream stage updates over Server-Sent Events.

6
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:48,000
The extraction finishes, but notice the status: Needs Review.

7
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:58,000
DataNova Extract doesn't blindly trust model outputs. Our deterministic arithmetic engine verified the math.

8
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:09,000
It caught that the stated grand total was five hundred euros higher than the sum of items and tax.

9
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:17,500
Pressing 'R' enters Review Mode. Hovering over any field highlights its exact visual bounding box on the source document.

10
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:28,000
We correct the total to two thousand nine hundred seventy-five euros. Instantly, the arithmetic reconciles.

11
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:37,000
The document status upgrades to Approved, and Nova celebrates.

12
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:46,000
We can now export directly to Excel with native formulas, CSV, or an audit-ready PDF.

13
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:56,000
In production, high volume matters. Our batch queue handles up to 20 documents simultaneously.

14
00:01:56,500 --> 00:02:07,000
We support non-Latin scripts including Devanagari Hindi GST, Arabic Right-to-Left, Tamil, and CJK.

15
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:18,000
Under the hood, LangGraph orchestrates specialized Vision, Extractor, and Judge agents.

16
00:02:18,500 --> 00:02:27,000
Reinforced by strict client-side cost controls and a zero-drift math validator.

17
00:02:27,500 --> 00:02:35,000
Try it yourself right now at uni-lang.vercel.app.
